# RC-003 — Resilient Experience

North star: **Reliable, calm, carefully crafted — even on poor network.**

## Before shipping or changing user flows ask

- Does every loading state feel intentional — no blank screens?
- Do errors explain simply with a recovery action — no technical messages?
- Do empty states gently guide — never feel unfinished?
- Are controllers disposed and async gaps guarded with `mounted`?
- Do critical actions have Semantics labels and adequate touch targets?

If any answer is no — revise.

## Canonical doc

`docs/RC-003.md`

## Out of scope

UI redesign · new features

## Success

First-time and offline users both feel ORACLY is trustworthy.
